<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/005e304b458e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide provides IT support services to Catholic Health, helping manage its technology needs and operations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5001" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0b8753486d6b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5002] The company has said that under US law, consumers are entitled to one free credit report annually via Equifax, Experian, and TransUnion." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5002" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0d26ad769bf7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4991] Serviceaide, Inc., a San Jose, California-based business associate that offers agentic AI-powered agents for IT and workflow management..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4991" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1241f0f91223> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4943] Serviceaide is a provider of informationtechnology support management services to Catholic Health. [4994] ...Serviceaide, which provides AI-driven chatbots and IT support solutions, was contracted by Catholic Health..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4943" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/13d3a1e2633f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4994] ...Serviceaide, which provides AI-driven chatbots and IT support solutions, was contracted by Catholic Health and entrusted with managing protected health information..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4994" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1a31cfbb935b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide learned of suspicious activity on its network on or about November 15, 2024." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5001" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2511d0bd9627> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4943] Serviceaide is a provider of informationtechnology support management services to Catholic Health. [4994] ...Serviceaide, which provides AI-driven chatbots and IT support solutions, was contracted by Catholic Health..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4943" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/258e4bcfa8fb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4994] AI service provider Serviceaide Inc. faces two proposed class action lawsuits from a data breach tied to Catholic Health System Inc." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4994" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/26350e813601> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4994] ...Serviceaide, which provides AI-driven chatbots and IT support solutions, was contracted by Catholic Health and entrusted with managing protected health information..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4994" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2858758b2eac> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "However, information from the US Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) shows that over 483,000 individuals were affected." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5002" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2f4766a23bfd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Unsecured Serviceaide Database Exposed Data of 483,000 Catholic Health Patients" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4991" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4333ed9a16ca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4997] The U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) is reviewing the breach under HIPAA's third-party vendor compliance guidelines. [4999] Aligning with government and industry frameworks, such as those from CISA, NIST and HIPAA, is critical to ensuring strong security practices." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4997" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4e3605b7a8e2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4993] IT services company Serviceaide notified the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) on May 9 that the sensitive data of up to 483,126 Catholic Health patients may have been exposed in a breach." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4993" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/53343bec294a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5002] The company has said that under US law, consumers are entitled to one free credit report annually via Equifax, Experian, and TransUnion." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5002" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/63e4db48dad6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4942] HHS' Office for Civil Rights fined Puerto Rico-based clearinghouse Inmediata Health Group $250,000 as part of a HIPAA settlement involving such an incident in 2019." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4942" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/65bf30ef45fc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Agentic AI Tech Firm Says Health Data Leak Affects 483,000" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4942" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6a811bad829c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Enterprise management solutions provider Serviceaide has informed the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) that a data leak impacts the personal and medical information of nearly half a million Catholic Health patients." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4995" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6ae44fff91f1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4999] Aligning with government and industry frameworks, such as those from CISA, NIST and HIPAA, is critical to ensuring strong security practices." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4999" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7188d3dab6f9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide informed the HHS, according to the government organization's incident tracker, that just over 483,000 individuals are impacted by the data breach." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4995" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7660efc67aa3> a airo:Evidence ;
