<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0efc6ba671b3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide, Inc., a San Jose, California-based business associate that offers agentic AI-powered agents for IT and workflow management, has announced a major data breach affecting almost half a million patients of the six-hospital healthcare system, Catholic Health in Buffalo, New York." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4991" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/28170df23045> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On or around November 15, 2024, Serviceaide discovered that certain information within its Catholic Health Elasticsearch database had been accidentally exposed and made publicly available." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5001" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/38b423fb1511> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A misconfigured database at enterprise IT provider Serviceaide has exposed sensitive health and personal information belonging to approximately 500,000 patients linked to Catholic Health." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4996" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/583d4ff8efdc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Notably, the database contained psychiatric treatment notes and prescription records, which are protected under stricter regulations like 42 CFR Part 2." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4997" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5a8bcd5405ac> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "HIPAA-regulated entities should ensure they have policies and procedures for checking authentication controls on cloud-based storage, as exposed databases are a common cause of data breaches." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4991" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7579e1c97e1a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "AI service provider Serviceaide Inc. faces two proposed class action lawsuits from a data breach tied to Catholic Health System Inc., a nonprofit hospital network in Buffalo, New York." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4994" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8ba48981633a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "If you're a Catholic Health patient, your private medical information may have been exposed in a data breach." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4992" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/af8c3f43a7a4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On November 15, 2024, Serviceaide learned that certain information within its Catholic Health Elasticsearch database was inadvertently made publicly available." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4943" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eb31fd7e3eee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The lawsuits allege claims of negligence, breach of implied contract, unjust enrichment, invasion of privacy, and violations of California's Unfair Competition Law." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4994" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eb7711a20c56> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On November 15, 2024, Serviceaide discovered that certain information within its Catholic Health Elasticsearch database had been exposed online and could be accessed without authentication." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4991" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f3581125a93c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide, a provider of agentic artificial intelligence-based IT management and workflow software, reported to regulators that an inadvertent exposure of data on the web has affected more than 483,000 patients of client Catholic Health." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4942" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/881bfeeeab34> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide, Inc., a San Jose, California-based business associate that offers agentic AI-powered agents for IT and workflow management, has announced a major data breach affecting almost half a million patients of the six-hospital healthcare system, Catholic Health in Buffalo, New York." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4991" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d42956b9050e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) is reviewing the breach under HIPAA's third-party vendor compliance guidelines." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4997" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29a775a06d90> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide has recently mailed notification letters to the affected individuals and informed the HHS' Office for Civil Rights about the data breach on May 9, 2025." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4991" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2cd20c011c51> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Filed in the U.S. District Court for the Northern District of California, the lawsuits allege that Serviceaide acted negligently and failed to protect sensitive data in its Elasticsearch database that was made publicly accessible allegedly for months before being disclosed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4994" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e36e0776bae> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Edelson Lechtzin LLP is investigating claims regarding data privacy violations at Serviceaide (\"Serviceaide\")." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5001" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3251048ccb37> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "HHS' Office for Civil Rights fined Puerto Rico-based clearinghouse Inmediata Health Group $250,000 as part of a HIPAA settlement involving such an incident in 2019." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4942" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/935c9929b5b4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The incident was reported to the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services Office for Civil Rights where Serviceaide said it has identified at least 483,126 individuals impacted by the incident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5000" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a16229c5fcbd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide is offering 24 months of credit monitoring via Experian IdentityWorks, but critics argue this fails to address medical identity theft risks." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4997" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e0fe084c360c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Federal Trade Commission may be reached at: 600 Pennsylvania Avenue NW, Washington, DC 20580." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4943" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/085ed704384f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The company informed the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4999" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5aee02d5a1e4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tech support company Serviceaide, which handles data services for Catholic Health, said between September and November 2024, certain health information like prescriptions and treatments were made publicly available." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4992" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/62b177fe01d1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It is also working with federal regulators, including the Department of Health and Human Services, which lists the breach publicly on its Office for Civil Rights breach portal." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4996" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c6957e25563d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide is a provider of informationtechnology support management services to Catholic Health." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4943" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c745a836ad30> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We are also notifying appropriate government regulators, including the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4943" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d09a9e58a53f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "If you're a Catholic Health patient, your private medical information may have been exposed in a data breach." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4992" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d80299437591> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Serviceaide,Inc. (\"Serviceaide\") is providing notice of an incident that may have impacted the privacy of certain individuals' information." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4943" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6c4108eced34> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Aligning with government and industry frameworks, such as those from CISA, NIST and HIPAA, is critical to ensuring strong security practices." ;
